served the community for 69 years. Early improvements included a new
child development center building in 1971, and a classroom building and
restroom building in 1975. Further improvements included a new library
building and lunch court shelter in 2004, and heating and cooling upgrades
in 2019. In 2024 the modernization included existing classroom buildings
and the administration building.
Proposed Improvements
Transitional kindergarten classrooms, restrooms, and playgrounds to be
renovated or newly constructed.
Additional projects will include expanded and improved facilities for special
education, updated classroom instructional technology, and modernized
wired and wireless network infrastructure. Campus safety and health
improvements will include additional exterior lighting to increase student
safety and facilitate expanded after-school programs.
Energy-efficiency improvements include solar energy and battery storage
systems. Other sustainable upgrades to include electric vehicle charging
stations to support the district’s clean transportation goals, and LED lighting
to reduce energy consumption and greenhouse gas emissions.
Secure campus improvements will provide perimeter and interior security
fencing, secure gates and door locks and hardware. Additional solutions
include security camera systems and lighting to illuminate student walkways
and building entrances.
Whitman Elementary School
Prior Improvements
Whitman Elementary School was originally constructed in 1956 and has
served the community for 70 years. Improvements included modernization
of existing classroom buildings in 2003, heating and cooling upgrades in
